  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name, usually a middle name, then the family name. Most family names are English, Scottish and Irish, and first names get shortened fast (Lachlan to Lachie, Thomas to Tommo). Post-war migration brought large Italian and Greek communities, especially in Melbourne, then Lebanese families in south-west Sydney and Vietnamese families in Cabramatta, Footscray and Springvale; more recently many Chinese and Indian Australians. Second-generation Greek and Italian Australians often have an English everyday name (Con for Konstantinos, Nick, Tina). First Nations people mostly carry English names.",
